From 8bcb438d888cd1a536e8fec8edc277a269d67a0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:26:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] UML-ANDROID-LOCAL: share GPU buffers as blob resources

A classic 3D resource lives inside the context that created it and has no
handle the renderer can export, so a second context cannot open it. The
Vulkan driver imports gralloc buffers exactly that way, and every import
failed here with "invalid res_id" because the allocator had created a
classic resource.

The driver only considered a blob when host_gbm_enabled was set, which it
derives from whether the host implements NV12 natively. That probe asks
whether the host allocator is minigbm; it says nothing about whether blob
resources work, and a host with a different allocator fails it while
supporting blobs perfectly well. Allocate a blob for any buffer the GPU
shares, and leave the probe gating only the rules that really describe the
other host. The caller has already established that the device offers blob
resources and a host-visible window.

Change-Id: Id05472c5fa529fa59965f563f41d1c7bc491a10e
---
 virtgpu_virgl.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/virtgpu_virgl.c b/virtgpu_virgl.c
index 7d798aeef29dff3b7fb7a4714f765e62c61721a9..73b6003dbfe5fb8c0ffa808b5097182060f23c52 100644
--- a/virtgpu_virgl.c
+++ b/virtgpu_virgl.c
@@ -972,7 +972,22 @@ static bool should_use_blob(struct driver *drv, uint32_t format, uint64_t use_fl
 {
 	struct virgl_priv *priv = (struct virgl_priv *)drv->priv;
 
-	// Only use blob when host gbm is available
+	/*
+	 * Only a blob resource carries a handle the renderer can hand to a
+	 * second context, so a buffer the GPU shares has to be one: the Vulkan
+	 * driver imports gralloc buffers that way, and a classic 3D resource
+	 * has nothing to export. The caller already established that the
+	 * device offers blob resources and a host-visible window.
+	 */
+	if (use_flags & (BO_USE_RENDERING | BO_USE_SCANOUT | BO_USE_TEXTURE))
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * The remaining rules describe a host whose allocator is minigbm, which
+	 * this driver detects by asking whether the host implements YUV natively
+	 * rather than emulating it. That probe says nothing about whether blob
+	 * resources work, so it stays where it is and gates only its own rules.
+	 */
 	if (!priv->host_gbm_enabled)
 		return false;
 
